Henri stands close beside the kitchen counter and holds a round wooden clock with both hands right in front of his squinting eyes, leaning his head forward to inspect the dial. The elderly man has short combed white wavy hair, a soft jawline, a full white beard and moustache, brown eyes, a small mole under his left eye, and a small mole on his right cheek, dressed in a brown wool cardigan over a cream collared shirt and grey trousers. His black-framed reading glasses are missing from his face, resting flat on the worn pale wooden counter near a bread bin and ceramic jug. Through the window beside the counter, the dim garden lawn and autumn maple leaves are visible in the dusk light. Close-up shot framed from the waist up, focusing on Henri's furrowed face and the ticking clock face held inches from his nose.

---METADATA---
