Marc stands in the open terrace doorway and extends both hands forward, presenting a thick folded pale blue bath towel toward Léa, who turns her head away from the dark lawn to look up at the soft cloth. Marc is an adult man with short combed dark brown wavy hair parted on the side, brown eyes, light stubble on his jaw, wearing a blue checked flannel shirt with sleeves rolled up, blue jeans, and brown leather boots. Standing just inside the threshold behind him, Élodie watches attentively in her long yellow cardigan and slim brown trousers, her light brown hair resting over her shoulders. The warm glow of the kitchen illuminates the grey stone terrace outside, where red and yellow autumn leaves lie scattered across the threshold in the cool evening breeze. Medium shot framed through the doorway showing the exchange of the folded towel.

---METADATA---
