Léa walks steadily across the damp green grass in her thick yellow-grey knitted wool socks, holding the folded pale blue bath towel bundled firmly against her chest with both arms. The small toddler girl wears her buttoned red flannel pyjamas, her straight dark brown hair blowing slightly as she moves into the dark garden toward the distant timber shed. Behind her on the terrace, Marc grips the white metal railing with both hands, leaning forward in his blue checked shirt and jeans to watch her progress, illuminated by the steady beam of a black flashlight cutting across the autumn lawn. At the far edge of the garden in the background, Pic the hedgehog rests motionless at the dark gap beneath the shed, tiny ears alert. Wide shot capturing the expansive dark lawn, the light beam guiding Léa's steps, and the waiting shed.

