Léa kneels down on the damp earth at the base of the weathered timber shed, extending her arms forward to hold the folded pale blue bath towel toward the shadowy gap in the brickwork. The toddler girl is framed from the waist up in her red flannel pyjamas, her chin-length dark brown hair falling softly beside her focused cheeks as her warm brown eyes look directly into the recess. Deep inside the dark opening, Pic the hedgehog pulls back into the shadows, only his soft cream-coloured snout, dark pink nose tip, and shiny round dark eyes visible as he refuses to emerge. Fallen red and gold maple leaves lie scattered over the soil and short grass along the edge of the shed's foundation. Close-up shot focusing on Léa's gentle outreach and the hedgehog's cautious face hidden in the dark gap.

---METADATA---
