Seen over the shoulder of Léa, who kneels in the foreground on the damp ground, Pic the hedgehog steps forward from the dark recess and bites the corner of the pale blue bath towel with his teeth, pulling the soft looped cloth into his shelter. Léa is cropped in the front corner showing the back of her head, dark straight chin-length hair, and the shoulder of her red flannel pyjamas. Just inside the opening beneath the weathered shed boards, Pic's cream-coloured face and bright round eyes beam with contentment as his small soft paws tug the warm terry-cloth towel deeper across the packed soil. A few golden autumn maple leaves rest near the edge of the brick plinth under the dim evening light. Over-the-shoulder shot looking down from beside Léa's shoulder into the illuminated mouth of the hedgehog's nest.

---METADATA---
