Pic the hedgehog pushes the pale grey plush rabbit out from the dark shed gap using his soft cream snout, nudging it directly into Léa's waiting hands as she kneels on the damp earth. The little toddler girl beams with joy, her round face lit with delight, brown eyes shining, and chin-length dark hair falling forward as her fingers close tightly around the soft body and floppy pink-lined ears of her beloved toy rabbit. Beside the weathered timber boards, Pic looks up with bright round dark eyes and a soft, rounded snout, settled comfortably beside his newly acquired warm blue towel inside the recess. Scattered autumn maple leaves dust the ground beside the brick foundation in the quiet evening air. Close-up shot showing Léa's joyful embrace of the rabbit and the friendly hedgehog at the threshold of the gap.

